# Escape from the Forbidden City (Peter Edwards, ASL v550) — WINNING
#   walkthrough, override-only (no published walkthrough exists). A fantasy
#   rescue quest through a walled city, seaside and mountains: three tasks
#   set by a warning note — place a jewel in the temple socket, burn a
#   talisman, and free a princess from a dragon-guarded dungeon — culminate
#   in delivering her to her father at the beautiful lake. Oracle reports
#   state=Finished errors=0, steps=115, scriptExhausted=True.
# Route: from the cell, north to the street then into the hardware shop
#   (look at shelf; take/wear gloves — needed to handle nettles safely) and
#   back out. West through the Park of Tranquility to the north end of Well
#   Street; search the nettles for a hidden brick, then take it and the key
#   that's revealed alongside it. Backtrack to the old wooden door and kick
#   it open (a key never fits it) to reach the Well Room. Push the coil of
#   rope to rig a way down, enter the well — carrying the brick keeps you
#   from drowning — take the jewel, drop the brick (it floats you back to
#   the surface) and climb the rope out.
# South to the Temple Road; unlock the temple doors with the key and put
#   the jewel in the socket — this both completes task 1 and silently opens
#   a new bridge crossing north of the Park (removing a snake/hawk
#   roadblock) for later. Back out and north through that new crossing to
#   the clearing; `look at fountain` clears its hidden-contents flag so the
#   gold coin can then be taken (a plain `open fountain` fails — the
#   fountain's open/close verbs are hardcoded off even though it's listed
#   as an option). West into the woods: climb the Rugbug tree, then go
#   down (the bark you dislodge falls to the room below, not with you),
#   take the bark and chew it to shrink yourself. West to the gloomy
#   corner and feel in the hole (only works while shrunk) to retrieve the
#   talisman from inside a beech tree. Backtrack east three times and burn
#   the talisman — task 2 done, opening a passage south from the cell.
# Southward through the Temple Road/junction area to the apothecary shop;
#   open the box and buy the wyrm pill with the gold coin. Back out and
#   south/west to the beach; search the stones for a hidden sharp flint and
#   take it. East to the moored boat and cut its knot with the flint,
#   freeing it. West to the pier, enter the boat and sail south three times
#   to the rocky shore (custom exit scripts auto-ferry the boat while
#   "aboard"); leave the boat before going further south, since it can't
#   reach the waterfall by boat. Look at the waterfall to reveal a hidden
#   cave behind it, then south and east to find the blowpipe; load it with
#   the wyrm pill.
# West/west/north to fetch the hairpin, then south/west into the dragon's
#   cave and wait four turns for the sleeping dragon to progress to
#   yawning (waiting a turn further without acting is fatal) before blowing
#   the loaded blowpipe to kill it, opening the dungeon to the south. Pick
#   the lock with the hairpin and take the princess — task 3 done. South to
#   the cavern and push the slab to open a shortcut tunnel south, then
#   south twice more to the beautiful lake, where the king and citizens
#   welcome the princess home for the winning ending.
